id: pm-cxc4jc
title: Serialize the complete build pipeline so overlapping validation cannot consume partially rewritten dist artifacts
description: Concurrent build producers can overlap TypeScript output rewriting and bundling. During packed first-run validation the bundler reported exported nested-settings symbols as undefined while another build was rewriting dist. Serialize the complete producer pipeline and make consumers wait for a settled artifact generation; do not rely on invocation discipline alone.
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-16T11:59:11.360Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-17T05:04:31.293Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-17T04:56:22.872Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-17T04:56:22.872Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Two overlapping builds produce identical complete artifacts; concurrent test consumers cannot observe partial dist files; regression uses real overlapping processes and checks exported symbols
parent: pm-u9d0
resolution: "Serialize prepare, TypeScript compilation, bundling and finalization under one checkout lease; hold that lease through sandboxed tests and coverage; reject incomplete generations and reentrant producers"
expected_result: Overlapping builds and test consumers observe complete exported artifacts and preserve failure evidence
actual_result: Two overlapping full builds produced the same 92-file generation; an independent process imported the completed export only after publication; 8928 tests passed at exact 100/100/100/100 and linked acceptance passed
