comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-16T11:59:11.360Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete 2762-item full all-status export plus keyword search and exact phrase scan found historical overlapping-build observations in pm-7vr0, pm-utxk3h, pm-nrkjik, pm-xau3 and pm-998juj, but no dedicated owner for serializing the entire producer pipeline. Existing parent lineage reused. This follow-up stays open while current delivery uses serialized producers."
  "2026-09-17T04:17:00.379Z","harness:codex","Design: one exclusive checkout lease covers prepare, TypeScript, bundles and finalization. Test consumers hold the same lease through Vitest and coverage checks. Nested read-only runners may inherit a verified lease; builds inside a consumer lease are refused. No age-based lock stealing; interrupted builds leave an incomplete marker and prebuilt consumers require a successful rebuild. Real independent-process tests will prove overlap and failure behavior."
  "2026-09-17T04:28:38.692Z","harness:codex","Validation toolchain refresh: pnpm updated eslint-plugin-sonarjs 4.2.0 to 4.2.1, fast-check 4.10.0 to 4.10.1, and jscpd 5.2.0 to 5.2.1 under normal supply-chain age policy. Complete all-status inventory reused the existing major-migration owners pm-do5b, pm-fokyhh and pm-ksr40d; current registry peer/engine contracts still exclude their respective TypeScript 7, Vitest 5 and npm-package-arg 14 upgrades."
  "2026-09-17T04:34:26.877Z","harness:codex",Full-suite validation exposed inherited consumer receipts crossing into isolated regression checkout copies. Clearing that receipt at the disposable-checkout boundary preserves independent ownership and lets real negative controls execute. New executable entrypoints are directly tested without adding coverage exclusions.
  "2026-09-17T04:44:22.506Z","harness:codex","Validation update: 105 focused tests passed across build ownership, test runner, registry controls, lifecycle negative controls, docs and parsed workflow contracts. Five changed executable scripts have exact coverage: statements 234/234, branches 180/180, functions 28/28, lines 220/220, with no new coverage exclusions. Two real overlapping full builds completed after the active coverage consumer released its lease and retained identical bundle generation 34f6db38b64ff182003a011de27520097e163eb6302bc5bfcd3a84184d9764ad across 92 files. Repository-wide ESLint, zero-clone duplication, typecheck and secret scan passed; full rerun is pending."
  "2026-09-17T04:55:58.627Z","harness:codex","Final local verification: all 8928 tests in 701 files passed; exact coverage statements 64706/64706, branches 49353/49353, functions 13434/13434, lines 61942/61942. PM-linked six-file run passed 39 tests with zero failure categories. Strengthened the real independent-process lease regression to import and assert the complete exported symbol after publication; all four lease regressions pass. Producer and consumer ownership behavior is verified without weakening coverage, output or lifecycle gates."
  "2026-09-17T05:04:31.293Z","harness:codex","Graph provenance correction: the compatible-only toolchain refresh decision was derived from the three linked canonical migration investigations. These discovered_from edges record that decision source; they do not assert that the migrations were implemented or that they block the completed build serialization. The unchanged prose-edge gate detected the missing structured provenance."
